  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>A warning first</h2>
      <p><strong>This lake is not an outing for your dog.</strong> The regulation published by the Provence Verte &amp; Verdon tourist office for Lac Sainte-Suzanne, known as "Lac de Carcès", is explicit: "pets banned around the lake".</p>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Nestled among the wooded hills of the Provence Verte, 3.5 km from Carcès and 4.5 km from Cabasse, this body of water is entirely devoted to walking and fishing: jogging, picnics, cycling, nature discovery and birdwatching. A dam was built between 1933 and 1935 to supply drinking water to the Toulon area; the reservoir can store up to 8 million m³. The site is Natura 2000 classified.</p>
      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme listing specifies that pets are banned around the lake "by inter-prefectoral order". Besides this ban, the site's regulation bans access to the water, swimming and boating on the lake (it is a drinking-water reserve for Toulon), wild camping, barbecues and fires, and flying recreational drones. Only line fishing is allowed, no-kill for carp and black bass. Access to the site is also subject to the summer restrictions on access to forest massifs. The lake car park is on the D24, towards Vins-sur-Caramy.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Coco can't come along here, even on a leash. For a freshwater outing in the Var with your dog, look at the other listings in the area instead.</div>
      <h2>Access, season and works</h2>
      <p>The lake is open every day from October to May. From June to September, walking, picnics and fishing on the "lake track" and along the D13 are regulated by the prefecture because of fire risk: the interactive map at risque-prevention-incendie.fr/var is updated every evening at 6pm, and a risk of the lake drying out is reported. The lake track, on the left bank, is only 2.5 km from the car park to the dam (about 1h30 there and back), as it is not possible to walk all the way round the lake; it can also be done with a pushchair. The tourist office announces a second draining of the dam in October-November 2027, for a period of two years.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of Carcès and the Caramy falls are close by; check their dog rules before going.</p>
